{"id":"chatcmpl-efb7bd97-b1a6-4ff3-bff1-7aaa9d0ef07a","object":"chat.completion","created":1795245319,"model":"deepseek-v4.1-flash","choices":[{"index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","reasoning_content":"","content":"```json\n{\n  \"highlights\": \"This task demonstrates a domain-expert delegation pattern for medical image interpretation, where a specialized tool is queried with a targeted diagnostic question rather than a generic description request. A verification step is inserted before finalizing the answer to resolve a known ambiguity (naming convention vs. image orientation). The pattern generalizes to any task requiring expert interpretation plus a convention-sensitive answer mapping.\",\n  \"patterns\": [\n    \"Delegate image interpretation to a domain-specific expert tool with a question framed around the discriminating feature (e.g., direction of convexity), not a generic 'describe the image' prompt.\",\n    \"When the answer depends on a naming convention (e.g., laterality defined by convexity side) and image orientation markers, insert an explicit verification step before committing to an option.\",\n    \"Map expert findings to answer options by confirming the convention-to-option correspondence, rather than assuming the expert's phrasing matches the option label.\",\n    \"Use a two-stage flow: (1) extract the discriminating finding via expert tool, (2) validate the finding-to-option mapping against orientation/convention risks.\"\n  ],\n  \"playbooks\": {\n    \"Medical imaging multiple-choice\": \"Query a modality-specific expert with a question targeting the single discriminating feature; then verify laterality/orientation conventions before selecting the option.\",\n    \"Convention-sensitive classification\": \"Identify whether the label depends on a convention (side of convexity, handedness, coordinate frame) and add a mapping-check step between raw finding and option label.\",\n    \"Expert-tool orchestration\": \"Frame expert queries around the decision boundary (left vs right, present vs absent) rather than open-ended description to reduce ambiguity in downstream mapping.\"\n  },\n  \"checklists\": [\n    \"Confirm the expert's reported finding (e.g., 'right convexity') maps correctly to the option wording under the stated naming convention.\",\n    \"Verify image orientation markers (e.g., R/L marker placement) were correctly interpreted before finalizing laterality.\"\n  ]\n}\n```"},"finish_reason":"stop","logprobs":null}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":488,"total_tokens":904,"completion_tokens":416,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0,"image_tokens":0,"text_tokens":488},"completion_tokens_details":{"text_tokens":416}}}